  "aiContextParagraph": "The discussion regarding the Indonesian vice presidency began when DPD RI Chair Sultan Najamudin publicly introduced the concept of appointing three individuals to the role. According to media reports, Najamudin suggested that this structural shift could serve as a model for future leadership, though he explicitly noted that the proposal is not intended for the current administration under President Prabowo. While the idea of multiple vice presidents has gained attention in national discourse, some reports highlight that this is not an entirely new concept within political circles. The DPD RI leadership continues to emphasize the need for open public deliberation to explore how such administrative changes might impact the nation's governance. This initiative remains a topic of academic and political speculation, with officials framing it as a contribution to the evolution of Indonesia’s leadership framework.",
